r.t:
• Identify location-based opportunities for LED, including in the low carbon economy; Facilitate diverse economic opportunities by allowing small business unit sizes, plan for mixed use areas; 
• Identify risk zones and mark risky areas 
• Consider safe conditions for economic growth in land use and infrastructure planning 
• Facilitate diverse economic opportunities by allowing small business unit sizes, plan for mixed use areas;

• Safeguard critical assets and utilities part of the planning process
• Locate any new critical assets and utilities outside of high-risk zones
• Ensure minimum accessibility of the settlement accessible in all weather conditions (access to/and within) for emergency vehicles and public transport;

• Require adequate percentage and distribution of vegetative ground cover and closed canopy to mitigate extreme heat; 
• Road upgrading must be planned in a way to minimize/ avoid cutting down of trees in the road corridor
• There shall be nature-based solutions with respect to natural ecosystems, storm water flow path and ground water and soil conditions.

• Combine vegetative soil stabilization measures with adaptive road network planning and storm water management planning; 
• minimize road network density; minimize road network on steep terrain 
• Major road network increase shall be avoided on clayey soils and steep slopes
